      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import requests; r=requests.get('http://api.devnet.solana.com',timeout=15); print(r.status_code, r.text[:300])\" 2>&1 | tail -20\n",
      "duration": 20
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import requests; r=requests.get('https://example.com',timeout=15); print('example.com', r.status_code)\" 2>&1 | tail -5\n",
      "duration": 20
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Key findings: DNS resolves api.devnet.solana.com to 192.133.77.189. A plain HTTP GET to it returned 502 (something is listening and responding, likely a transparent gateway/proxy), while HTTPS to example.com works fine. So general HTTPS works, but the Solana host is intercepted by a middlebox that speaks plain HTTP (WRONG_VERSION_NUMBER on HTTPS, 502 on HTTP GET). I should investigate the environment for any configured RPC endpoint (local validator, proxy, env var, config file) and test an HTTP POST to the Solana RPC.",
  "plan": "1) Test an HTTP POST to http://api.devnet.solana.com (JSON-RPC needs POST, the GET 502 may just be wrong method). 2) Inspect /etc/hosts and look for any local RPC / config hints (README, env files, a validator). 3) Check for any listening local ports. This clarifies how to reach the chain.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import requests; r=requests.post('http://api.devnet.solana.com',json={'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':1,'method':'getSlot'},timeout=15); print(r.status_code, r.text[:400])\" 2>&1 | tail -20\n",
      "duration": 20
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /etc/hosts; echo '---'; ls -la /app; echo '---'; env | grep -iE 'solana|rpc|chain|net' \n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

